**Two separate Hermes realities — don't conflate them.**

### (a) The Mac runs its OWN local Hermes agent — usable as a brain ✅
- `which hermes` → `/Users/quantumcode/.local/bin/hermes`, a wrapper execing
  `~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/hermes`.
- Full Nous Research **hermes-agent** install at `~/.hermes/` (config.yaml, state.db,
  sessions, skills, memories, source).
- `~/.hermes/config.yaml`: `model.default: grok-4.3`, `provider: xai-oauth`,
  `base_url: https://api.x.ai/v1`; auth in `~/.hermes/auth.json` (names only).
- **Not currently paired/running:** `~/.hermes/pairing/` empty, `telegram.allowed_chats: ''`,
  no hermes process live. But invocable directly via the CLI.

### (b) The VPS Hermes gateway (187.124.251.98) — NO wired path from the Mac ✅
- The "Quantum Hermes" VPS docs at `AGENTSINFO/VPS_Agents/Quantum_Hermes/` are **unfilled
  templates**: `vps_connection.md` host/IP = "_(fill in)_"; `.env.example` all blank;
  `agent_config.yaml` provider `""`, status "🟡 In Setup". No real endpoint, no token.
- The only wired route to `187.124.251.98` is **Paperclip** (`PAPERCLIP/CLAUDE.md`):
  `VPS="root@187.124.251.98"`, dashboard `https://paperclip.billyrovzar.com/LEMA/dashboard`
